{"seconds": 57.5, "exit": 0, "final": "Perfect! So the line is:\n1. **Qh7+** (check, forcing Nxh7)\n2. **Nxh7** (Black's only legal move, capturing the queen)\n3. **Bxh7+** (White bishop takes the knight with check)\n4. **Kg7** or **Kh8** (Black must move the king)\n5. **Nxf7+** (White knight takes pawn with check, forking king and queen)\n\nThis is a **fork** and **pin** combination. The knight on f6 is pinned (it can't move because it's defending against Qh7+), and after the queen sacrifice, White exploits this with a forcing knight fork.\n\nLet me verify one more time the initial move appears in legal_moves (it does\u2014I saw it as Qh7+ in the checks list).\n\n**Best move: Qh7+**\n\nThe motif is **pin** (the Nf6 is pinned to the king) combined with a **sacrifice** that forces a winning tactical sequence.\n\n**Coaching note (coaching explanation):** \nWhen your opponent's knight on f6 is pinned to defending the king, look for sacrificial checks that exploit this. Here, Qh7+ forces Nxh7 (the only legal move), and after Bxh7+ followed by Nxf7+, you win the queen through a royal fork. The key lesson: a pinned piece that's your only defender is a target for tactical shots.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qh7+\", \"line\": [\"Qh7+\", \"Nxh7\", \"Bxh7+\", \"Kg7\", \"Nxf7+\", \"Kxf7\"], \"motifs\": [\"pin\", \"fork\", \"sacrifice\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13", "square": "h6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13", "square": "g5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3